# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VERSION C. `results/*` above ignores .json by default, and this repository has
# now been bitten four times by a runner writing a registered artefact that git
# then silently declined to track -- D17, e2-doe-d8, and twice more. These four
# are gate targets and registration evidence, so they are named here rather than
# left to `git add -f`, which works once and is forgotten by the next session.
#
# `versionc-gate-s010.json` is the C0 gate: 600 rows, the branch fires on it.
# `versionc-gate-analysis.json` carries the per-arm table and the regression.
# `versionc-detector-fit.json` is section 3.2's fitting set, and
# `versionc-detector-boundary.json` the proposed one-class rule. The last two are
# what any future freeze must be checked against, so losing them loses the
# provenance of the rule.
#
# The `.partial` siblings stay ignored ON PURPOSE: the whole point of the partial
# convention is that a half-finished file must not be stageable.
!results/versionc-gate-s010.json
!results/versionc-gate-analysis.json
!results/versionc-detector-fit.json
!results/versionc-detector-boundary.json
!results/versionc-form1-s010.json
!results/versionc-form1-s025.json
